<%# Android builds its home-screen icon from this; without it, it shrinks the
    iPhone icon onto a white disc. "maskable" lets it crop the icon edge to
    edge into its shape (the VB sits inside the circle every crop keeps).

    display "standalone": Chrome only offers to install a site that opens in its
    own window, and only an installed site gets the maskable icon. Links to
    other sites (reserving a class, directions) open in an in-app browser panel
    with a way back, on Android and iOS alike.

    Rails' own controller renders this, without the app's helpers, so they're
    called through ApplicationController. %>
<% helpers = ApplicationController.helpers %>
<% background = Site.instance.theme.variables["--bg"] %>
<% icons = [ 192, 512 ].flat_map { |size| %w[any maskable].map { |purpose| { src: helpers.app_icon_path(size), type: "image/png", sizes: "#{size}x#{size}", purpose: } } } %>
<%= raw JSON.pretty_generate(
  id: "/",
  name: "Valley Built CrossFit",
  short_name: "Valley Built",
  description: "Coached CrossFit classes for every body in Grain Valley, Missouri.",
  lang: "en",
  start_url: "/",
  scope: "/",
  display: "standalone",
  background_color: background,
  theme_color: background,
  icons:
) %>
